Abstract:
Metro Manila traffic, specifically in EDSA, needs to be simulated and analyzed in order to minimize waste and pollution. The purpose of this research is to compare different traffic simulation software and choose which is the most viable for the researchers to simulate traffic in EDSA. The software were compared based on the following criteria: (1) Open Source and Free Use, (2) Operating System Portability, (3) Creating traffic networks and associated vehicle patterns, (4) Quality of GUI and Documentation, (5) Simulation output (data and files), (6) Ability to simulate very large traffic networks, (7) Additional capabilities, and (8) CPU and Memory performance. SUMO, Vissim, and Aimsun were found to perform reasonably well and had common and unique features with different strengths and weaknesses.
