SECTION IX.
Conclusion

SUMO, Aimsun and Vissim can all provide reasonable results. All three simulation packages were found to perform reasonably well, but with limitations that should be understood before selecting one for network evaluation.

Vissim's ability to cope with large traffic networks makes it a good simulation package for simulating EDSA. The current traffic data provided by the Department of Transportation (DOTr), fits perfectly to the vehicle pattern techniques of Vissim.

In the end, there was no ranking of ‘best’ or ‘worst’ software. All three had common and unique features and different strengths and weaknesses. Knowing the data and the needs of the traffic network to be simulated is the key turning point to selecting a simulation package.

